fix(pip): Let thermal optics keep the 3DSS path, with no new files

The pack's own lens shader treats a thermal optic (s3ds_image_type >= 2, or scope_lense_thermal) as
"the engine will hand me a hot image": in its scope_svp > 0 branch it skips its grading AND its
infrared() path, and just displays the second view. Nothing in this engine can satisfy that. The
only way the engine can make a view hot is phase_heatvision(), which is a DEVICE effect: the bundled
heat vision shader's compute_lens_mask() accepts a 1/2/4 tube layout and returns 0 everywhere else,
and with no worn device the tube count is 0, so the pass writes a black frame. That is the measured
cause of both the black lens and the black screen a forced r__heatvision 1 produces.

The pack's working thermal model is the one its OWN shader runs on the 3DSS path: infrared() over
the G-buffer plus the heat map LUT and pixelation. An optic takes that path exactly when the engine
does not provide the second viewport, so for these optics the honest answer is no lens. The player
gets the thermal sight the pack authored, with the plain ADS zoom the 3DSS setup already gives, and
the engine needs no new shader file - which is also what the reference did: its SVP activation
(CWeapon::UpdateSecondVP, four conditions, none about imaging) and its phase_combine
(if (ps_r2_heatvision > 0) phase_heatvision(); unguarded on the SVP frame) show that the thermal look
was always the pack script's job, driven from a worn device, and never the optic's.

Implemented as a state rule, not a special case at the call sites: SvpScopeInputs gained
optic_thermal_image and svp_evaluate_scope() refuses the lens for it, so the single writer keeps
owning the decision and every consumer (scope_svp, the wide main view, the mouse ratio, the lens
creation) follows. Tests cover the new boundary (52 checks now). The second target set is not even
created for such an optic, so a thermal sight costs no VRAM and no second scene pass.

Every optic that declares a thermal image also carries s3ds_image_type, so the pack's shader does
have its thermal path on the 3DSS branch. The one exception is [vulcan], the only optic that is both
NVG (s3ds_image_type = 1) and scope_lense_thermal: its thermal channel needs the engine's heat pass,
which the heat vision mod's masked shader makes unusable without a device. That is the pack's own
packaging state, identical in the reference, and is recorded in the contract document.